course: dictionary
lesson: 7896
title: Rapid means very fast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rapid means very fast, or happening quickly. You can use it for a runner, a river, or a change that happens in a short time. «The rapid growth of the plant surprised everyone.» Here rapid tells you the plant grew very quickly.
explain: Rapids are a different word with a different job. Rapids are parts of a river where the water flows very fast over rocks. «In its roaring rapids the goliath tigerfish hunts with long dagger teeth.» Roaring tells you the rapids are loud and fierce, so they are not calm water.
explain: Rapid can also describe a body or a test. Rapid breathing means breathing very fast. A rapid test gives you an answer quickly. «REM sleep, short for rapid eye movement, is when most vivid dreams happen.» The eyes move quickly during this kind of sleep.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «very fast» in place of rapid. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Use the clues around the word, and a dictionary when you are still not sure.
fact: Rapid means very fast or happening quickly.
fact: Rapids are parts of a river where the water flows very fast over rocks.
fact: Rapid growth means growing very quickly, and rapid change means changing in a short time.
fact: Rapid breathing means breathing very fast.
fact: Rapids can be dangerous for swimmers because the water moves so fast.
exercise: «The rapid growth of the young plant surprised everyone.» What does rapid mean here? | *Very fast | Very small | Very cold | Very dark green
exercise: «The river rapids roared over the rocks.» What are the rapids? | *Parts of a river where the water flows very fast over rocks | A kind of fish | Bridges over the river | Very deep, still pools
exercise: «The rapid change in the weather made everyone pack up.» Find and copy the word that means very quick. | everyone | *rapid | change | weather
test: «REM sleep, short for rapid eye movement, is when most vivid dreams happen.» What does rapid mean in rapid eye movement? | Very sleepy | Very slow | *Very fast | Very quiet
test: Why are river rapids dangerous for swimmers? | The water is too warm | The water is too still | *The water flows very fast over rocks | Fish bite swimmers there
exam: In maths, a «rapid increase» means the numbers rise by a lot | Without any change | Slowly, one small step at a time | Over many years | *In a short time
